      "message": "@chriswailes: Something weird is happening about where it thinks it is getting libc++.so.1 from again. Look at this local build (from `out/dist/bin`). It\u0027s pointing to a very specific toolchain libc++.so.1 rather than one that should be nearby.\n\n```\nsrhines@ringworld:__:bin$ ldd rustc \n        linux-vdso.so.1 (0x00007ffe113f9000)\n        librustc_driver-9c0a6d65184bed3c.so \u003d\u003e /disk/android_trees/aosp-rust-toolchain/out/package/bin/./../lib/librustc_driver-9c0a6d65184bed3c.so (0x00007f4a85227000)\n        libstd-e2b5a9efc098561c.so \u003d\u003e /disk/android_trees/aosp-rust-toolchain/out/package/bin/./../lib/libstd-e2b5a9efc098561c.so (0x00007f4a8508d000)\n        libc.so.6 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6 (0x00007f4a84ea3000)\n        libdl.so.2 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libdl.so.2 (0x00007f4a84e9d000)\n        libpthread.so.0 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libpthread.so.0 (0x00007f4a84e7a000)\n        libm.so.6 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so.6 (0x00007f4a84d35000)\n        libz.so.1 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libz.so.1 (0x00007f4a84d18000)\n        libc++.so.1 \u003d\u003e /disk/android_trees/aosp-rust-toolchain/prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/clang-r433403/lib64/libc++.so.1 (0x00007f4a84c22000)\n        libgcc_s.so.1 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libgcc_s.so.1 (0x00007f4a84c08000)\n        /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 (0x00007f4a8bebb000)\n        librt.so.1 \u003d\u003e /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/librt.so.1 (0x00007f4a84bfb000)\n```\n\n\nAlso if I run llvm-readelf on rustc, I can see that the RUNPATH is wrong (`/../lib64` instead of `$ORIGIN/../lib64`).\n\n```\n  0x000000000000001d (RUNPATH)      Library runpath: [$ORIGIN/../lib:/disk/android_trees/aosp-rust-toolchain/prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/clang-r433403/lib64:/../lib64]\n```\n\nvs. 1.55.0 which shows:\n\n```\n  0x000000000000001d (RUNPATH)      Library runpath: [$ORIGIN/../lib:$ORIGIN/../lib64:/buildbot/src/android/rust-tool